---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

/*
 * Written to describe what this site actually does today, rather than a
 * downloaded template. The previous site's policy was an unedited template
 * that named support@landin.com as its contact.
 *
 * Revised 2026-11-09 when Google Tag Manager was added. It MUST be revised
 * again when any of these land: an enquiry form, a cookie banner, or any
 * consent category moving off `denied`. See docs/content-todo.md.
 *
 * The claims here are load-bearing. Everything this page says about Tag
 * Manager is true only while the Consent Mode defaults in BaseLayout stay
 * denied; change those and this copy is a false statement to a UK regulator,
 * not a stale sentence.
 */
const path = '/privacy-policy/';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | EeroCad';
const description =
  'What data this website collects, what EeroCad does with it, and the rights you have over it under UK GDPR.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', path },
];

const updated = '9 November 2026';
---

<PageLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  heading="Privacy"
  headingAccent="Policy"
  lead={`Last updated ${updated}.`}
  path={path}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <div class="prose-page max-w-2xl">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      This website loads Google Tag Manager, but it is set to store nothing
      until you agree to it, so no analytics or advertising cookies are set on
      your device today. The site has no forms. If you email us or book a call,
      we hold what you send us so we can reply. We do not sell or rent anyone's
      data.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <p>
      We load Google Tag Manager on every page. It is configured with Google
      Consent Mode, and every non-essential category &mdash; analytics,
      advertising, advertising personalisation and advertising user data
      &mdash; is set to <em>denied</em> by default. Nothing changes that
      default at present, so Tag Manager sets no cookie and reads nothing from
      your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Loading it does mean your browser requests a file from Google's servers
      at <span class="font-mono text-sm">googletagmanager.com</span>, and that
      request carries your IP address and browser details in the ordinary way
      any request does. Google processes that under its own terms. If we later
      turn on analytics properly, we will ask you first, and this page will say
      so before it happens.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider keeps standard server logs, which include IP
      addresses, for security and reliability purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site stores one item in your browser's session storage to remember
      that you have already seen the introductory animation. It contains no
      personal data, it is not shared with anyone, and it is cleared when you
      close the tab.
    </p>

    <h2>If you contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you email <a href="mailto:info@eerocad.com">info@eerocad.com</a> or call
      us, we keep your message and contact details so we can respond and, if we
      end up working together, to administer that work.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our booking link is hosted by Calendly. If you book a call, the details
      you enter there are processed by Calendly under their own privacy policy
      as well as being shared with us.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries that do not lead to work are kept for up to two years, in case
      you come back. Records relating to work we carry out are kept for as long
      as we are required to retain business and tax records.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under UK GDPR you can ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about
      you, ask us to correct it, ask us to delete it, or object to how we are
      using it. Email <a href="mailto:info@eerocad.com">info@eerocad.com</a> and
      we will respond within one month.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are not satisfied with our response you can complain to the
      Information Commissioner's Office at
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we add an enquiry form, or switch on analytics or advertising tracking
      rather than loading it in the denied state described above, this policy
      will be updated before that goes live, and a cookie notice will be added
      where one is required.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:info@eerocad.com"
        >info@eerocad.com</a
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
